{% note
   text="Linux persistence is the process of maintaining access to a system after the initial compromise, logout, reboot, or process termination.\n\nLinux has many legitimate mechanisms that can be abused for persistence." /%}

### Common Persistence Mechanisms

{% twoColumn
   left="Cron can execute commands automatically on a schedule.\n\nCommon locations:\n/etc/crontab\n/etc/cron.d/\n/etc/cron.hourly/\n/etc/cron.daily/\n/etc/cron.weekly/\n/etc/cron.monthly/\n\nUser crontabs can also be used for persistence."
   right="Systemd services and timers can execute programs during boot or at scheduled times.\n\nUseful areas to inspect:\n/etc/systemd/system/\n/usr/lib/systemd/system/\n\nPay attention to unusual ExecStart paths." /%}

{% twoColumn
   left="SSH public keys can provide persistent remote access.\n\nCommon location:\n\n~/.ssh/authorized_keys\n\nUnknown keys or unusual key options should be investigated."
   right="Shell startup files can execute commands when a user starts a shell.\n\nExamples:\n\n~/.bashrc\n~/.profile\n~/.bash_profile\n~/.zshrc\n/etc/profile" /%}

{% terminal
   title="persistence enumeration"
   commands=[{cmd: "crontab -l"}, {cmd: "sudo crontab -l"}, {cmd: "systemctl list-unit-files --type=service"}, {cmd: "systemctl list-timers --all"}, {cmd: "cat ~/.ssh/authorized_keys"}, {cmd: "find / -perm -4000 -type f 2>/dev/null"}] /%}

{% finding
   severity="informational"
   text="Look for:\n\n• Unexpected scheduled jobs\n• Unknown systemd services or timers\n• Unrecognized SSH keys\n• Suspicious commands in shell startup files\n• Unusual SUID/SGID binaries\n• Unexpected privileged accounts\n• Executables running from unusual locations" /%}

{% warning
   text="A suspicious command or file does not automatically mean malicious persistence.\n\nCheck ownership, permissions, execution context, and whether the configuration is expected on the system." /%}

{% tip
   text="Instead of asking \"Does this file look malicious?\", ask:\n\n\"What causes this to execute?\"\n\nFinding the execution mechanism usually makes the rest of the investigation much easier." /%}

{% callout
   text="PersistHunt turns these persistence surfaces into separate detectors and normalizes their observations into standardized findings for analysis and risk scoring." /%}
